      "writtenOn": "2014-02-25T04:13:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "filter seem redundant\n\nthe first part \u0027objectclass\u003d*\u0027 will match any objectclass so the second part \u0027objectclass\u003dldapsubentry\u0027 is redundant",
      "revId": "18217417079e19dcd390ee1e55d2d772b121afdd",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "AAAAXX//3hw\u003d",
        "filename": "keystone/common/ldap/core.py",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 485,
      "author": {
        "id": 9098
      },
      "writtenOn": "2014-04-25T17:04:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The \u0027ldapsubentry\u0027 objectclass is used to flag entries as operational.  As with operational attributes, an \u0027ldapsubentry\u0027 will not be returned unless you specifically ask for it.  If we only use \u0027objectclass\u003d*\u0027 here, the subentries will be left behind, causing deletion of the non-leaf entry to fail since it will still have children.",
      "parentUuid": "AAAAU3//uKI\u003d",
      "revId": "18217417079e19dcd390ee1e55d2d772b121afdd",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "AAAAU3//oyw\u003d",
        "filename": "keystone/common/ldap/core.py",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 485,
      "author": {
        "id": 9983
      },
      "writtenOn": "2014-08-15T15:41:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In some directory servers, entries with objectclass: ldapsubentry are hidden from LDAP search operations.  In order to request these entries, you have to explicitly request them by having the (objectclass\u003dldapsubentry) as part of the search filter.\nIf they are present, and you do not request them, the delete will fail with NOT_ALLOWED_ON_NONLEAF.",
      "parentUuid": "AAAAU3//uKI\u003d",
      "revId": "18217417079e19dcd390ee1e55d2d772b121afdd",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "AAAAU3//uCU\u003d",
        "filename": "keystone/common/ldap/core.py",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 486,
      "author": {
        "id": 1916
      },
      "writtenOn": "2014-02-25T04:13:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "also, if I am looking at the right doc, (objectclass\u003d*) is already the default so no need to specify it. For efficiency, you don\u0027t want all the attributes back. In this case, all you care are the DNs. Maybe you can simplify this?\n\nentries \u003d conn.search_s(dn, scope, attrslist\u003d[\u0027dn\u0027], attrsonly\u003d1)",
      "revId": "18217417079e19dcd390ee1e55d2d772b121afdd",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "AAAAXX//3kE\u003d",
        "filename": "keystone/common/ldap/core.py",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 486,
      "author": {
        "id": 9098
      },
      "writtenOn": "2014-04-25T17:04:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Asking for the \u00271.1\u0027 attribute causes no attributes to be returned.  It\u0027s basically the opposite of \u0027*\u0027.  See section 4.5.1.8 of RFC 4511 for details:\n\n   noattrs \u003d %x31.2E.31 ; \"1.1\"",
      "parentUuid": "AAAAU3//uCU\u003d",
      "revId": "18217417079e19dcd390ee1e55d2d772b121afdd",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "AAAAU3//oyI\u003d",
        "filename": "keystone/common/ldap/core.py",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 486,
      "author": {
        "id": 9983
      },
      "writtenOn": "2014-08-15T15:41:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e also, if I am looking at the right doc, (objectclass\u003d*) is already the default so no need to specify it.\n\nSee above.\n\n\u003e attrslist\u003d[\u0027dn\u0027]\n\n\u0027dn\u0027 isn\u0027t really an attribute.  The proper LDAP way to request that no attributes in the entry are returned is to specify the attribute \u00271.1\u0027 by OID.  This OID is guaranteed not to exist in any LDAP server.  It is a common idiom in the LDAP world.\n\n\u003e attrsonly\u003d1\n\nSince no attributes will be returned with \u00271.1\u0027, the attrsonly\u003d1 flag is a no-op and can be omitted.",
      "parentUuid": "AAAAU3//uCU\u003d",
      "revId": "18217417079e19dcd390ee1e55d2d772b121afdd",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "AAAAVn//+6U\u003d",
        "filename": "keystone/common/ldap/core.py",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 488,
      "author": {
        "id": 6486
      },
      "writtenOn": "2014-03-03T00:24:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The LDAP specification says that the results can come back in any order, see https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc4511#section-4.5.2 .\n\n The SearchResultEntry and SearchResultReference messages\n   may come in any order.\n\nSo reversing the order of the entries returned doesn\u0027t make any difference.",
      "revId": "18217417079e19dcd390ee1e55d2d772b121afdd",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
